Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `variant_disease_coloc.left_chrom` / `left_pos` / `left_ref` / `left_alt`: identify the GWAS variant ‘1_55029009_C_T’.  
• `variant_disease_coloc.right_gene_id`: keep only rows for gene ENSG00000169174.  
• `variant_disease_coloc.right_bio_feature`: keep only “IPSC”.  
• `variant_disease_coloc.coloc_h4` / `coloc_h3`: reliability filters (h4 > 0.8, h3 < 0.02).  
• `variant_disease_coloc.coloc_log2_h4_h3`: value to summarise (average, variance, max‑min).  
• `variant_disease_coloc.right_study`: QTL study we finally want for the max log2(h4/h3).  
• `variant_disease_coloc.left_study`: joins to GWAS study metadata.  
• `studies.trait_reported`: text filter ‑ must contain “…lesterol levels…”.  

